## 2. Commercial Use Prohibited

Unless you have obtained prior written authorization or a separate commercial license from the copyright holder, you may not use PiDeck, in whole or in substantial part, for any commercial purpose.

Commercial use includes, but is not limited to:

1. Selling PiDeck or modified versions of PiDeck;
2. Charging users for access to PiDeck;
3. Offering PiDeck as a paid SaaS, hosted service, cloud service, managed service, or subscription service;
4. Integrating PiDeck into a commercial software product or commercial platform;
5. Using PiDeck as a substantial component of a product or service offered for commercial advantage;
6. Redistributing, sublicensing, leasing, renting, or reselling PiDeck for commercial purposes;
7. Providing paid deployment, hosting, customization, or managed PiDeck services where PiDeck itself forms a substantial part of the commercial offering;
8. Removing PiDeck branding and redistributing substantially the same software under another name for commercial purposes.

Internal use by a commercial organization is also considered commercial use unless separately authorized by the copyright holder.

